{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774213477,"nonce":"+P2OMj8JhO0ezOw86LEbJhcUY1I=","title":"General hook system: per-repo per-auth-type hooks with configurable intervention points","message":"Generalize the post-merge rebuild into a configurable hook system:\n- Per-repo, per-auth-type hooks (e.g., for mandible repo + merge type → rebuild and restart)\n- The mandible self-rebuild hook is always-active (cannot be disabled)\n- User can add custom hooks for any repo + auth type combination\n- Future: more intervention points beyond just post-auth-completion (pre-merge, post-commit, on-failure, etc.)\n- Hook can be: shell command, script path, or SDK agent spawn\n- Configuration stored in Mandible settings DB, manageable via settings UI\n\nRelated: the npm install before build fix (main worktree node_modules can be stale after package.json changes land via merge).","files":null}]}